# ITDK MCP Documentation

This directory is the project’s second brain: durable context that helps a
new contributor understand why the server exists, how it is constrained, and
what remains to be done. Keep documents short, linked, and current; promote
important discoveries out of chat, issues, and code into the appropriate area.

## Start here

- [Plans](plans/README.md) — sequenced implementation work and its status.
- [Architecture](architecture/README.md) — system boundaries and technical
  design.
- [Contracts](contracts/README.md) — MCP tool and data-return contracts.
- [Data](data/README.md) — supplied database schema, query access patterns,
  and data constraints.
- [Operations](operations/README.md) — configuration, Docker, deployment, and
  incident-facing guidance.
- [Decisions](decisions/README.md) — concise records of consequential choices.

## Documentation conventions

- Plans are dated and actionable. Update their status as work is completed.
- Contract changes require corresponding implementation and test updates.
- Never copy secrets, connection strings, or values from `.env` into docs.
- Prefer links to a canonical document over duplicating its content.
